Two focused UX changes to make `GameBoardOverlay` feel like the Home Island hub: adds a subtle atmospheric background image, and repurposes the middle-left circle button to open the Home Egg Hatchery instead of the defunct `CountdownCalendarModal`.

## Island background scene
- Imports `HalloweenNight.webp` as `islandScenePlaceholder` (placeholder until dedicated island art lands)
- Inserts a `position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 0; pointer-events: none` layer as the first child of `.game-board-overlay__content` — renders beneath all existing UI, no z-index or click-handler impact
- Image at `opacity: 0.35`; the existing `rgba(1,6,20,0.86)` backdrop already provides darkening

## Daily Hatch → Home Egg Hatchery navigation
**`App.tsx`** — replaces the `onDailyHatchClick` handler body:
```tsx
// before
setShowGameBoardOverlay(false);
setReopenGameOverlayOnRewardClose(true);
setShowCalendarPlaceholder(true);

// after
setShowGameBoardOverlay(false);
window.location.href = '/level-worlds.html?level=1&openHatchery=1';
```
`CountdownCalendarModal` and its state are left in place — only the call site is changed.

**`IslandRunBoardPrototype.tsx`** — reads the `openHatchery` param at module load (same pattern as `IS_DEV_TIMER`) and auto-opens the hatchery panel after runtime-state hydration:
```ts
const OPEN_HATCHERY_ON_LOAD = typeof window !== 'undefined' &&
  new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('openHatchery') === '1';

useEffect(() => {
  if (!hasHydratedRuntimeState) return;
  if (OPEN_HATCHERY_ON_LOAD) {
    setActiveStopId('hatchery');          // existing state, no new variable
    const url = new URL(window.location.href);
    url.searchParams.delete('openHatchery');
    window.history.replaceState({}, '', url.toString());
  }
}, [hasHydratedRuntimeState]);
```

