<details>

<summary>Original prompt</summary>

> ## Goal
> Two focused changes to `GameBoardOverlay` to make it feel like the real Home Island hub:
> 
> 1. **Add a background island scene image** behind the overlay content
> 2. **Repurpose the middle-left circle button** (`onDailyHatchClick`) to open the Home Egg Hatchery instead of the outdated `CountdownCalendarModal`
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Change 1: Island background in `GameBoardOverlay`
> 
> ### File: `src/components/GameBoardOverlay.tsx`
> 
> Add an import for `HalloweenNight.webp` (the best available full-scene asset for now — placeholder until dedicated island art is added):
> 
> ```tsx
> import islandScenePlaceholder from '../assets/HalloweenNight.webp';
> ```
> 
> Then inside the returned JSX, add an island scene image layer **inside** `.game-board-overlay__content`, as the **first child** (before the topbar):
> 
> ```tsx
> {/* Island background scene — placeholder art, swap for island-specific webp when available */}
> <div className="game-board-overlay__island-scene" aria-hidden="true">
>   <img
>     src={islandScenePlaceholder}
>     alt=""
>     className="game-board-overlay__island-scene-img"
>   />
> </div>
> ```
> 
> ### File: `src/styles/game-board-overlay.css`
> 
> Append these styles:
> 
> ```css
> /* Island background scene */
> .game-board-overlay__island-scene {
>   position: absolute;
>   inset: 0;
>   z-index: 0;
>   pointer-events: none;
>   overflow: hidden;
>   display: flex;
>   align-items: center;
>   justify-content: center;
> }
> 
> .game-board-overlay__island-scene-img {
>   width: 100%;
>   height: 100%;
>   object-fit: cover;
>   object-position: center;
>   opacity: 0.35;
> }
> ```
> 
> The black backdrop (`rgba(1, 6, 20, 0.86)`) already provides darkening — the island image at 35% opacity gives a subtle atmospheric hint without overpowering the UI. All existing content layers have higher z-index values and will render on top correctly.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Change 2: Repurpose the middle-left circle (Daily Hatch → Home Egg Hatchery)
> 
> ### File: `src/App.tsx`
> 
> Find the `onDailyHatchClick` handler on `<GameBoardOverlay>` (currently calls `setShowCalendarPlaceholder(true)`):
> 
> ```tsx
> onDailyHatchClick={() => {
>   setShowGameBoardOverlay(false);
>   setReopenGameOverlayOnRewardClose(true);
>   setShowCalendarPlaceholder(true);
> }}
> ```
> 
> Replace it with a navigation to Island Run with the hatchery panel flag:
> 
> ```tsx
> onDailyHatchClick={() => {
>   setShowGameBoardOverlay(false);
>   window.location.href = '/level-worlds.html?level=1&openHatchery=1';
> }}
> ```
> 
> ### File: `src/features/gamification/level-worlds/components/IslandRunBoardPrototype.tsx`
> 
> **Step A** — Near the top of the file (where other URL params like `devTimer` are read), add:
> 
> ```typescript
> const OPEN_HATCHERY_ON_LOAD = typeof window !== 'undefined' &&
>   new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('openHatchery') === '1';
> ```
> 
> **Step B** — Search the file for the state variable that controls the hatchery panel visibility (search for `hatchery` — it will be something like `showHatchery`, `hatcheryOpen`, etc.). Use whatever name is already there.
> 
> **Step C** — Add a `useEffect` that fires after hydration and auto-opens the hatchery if the flag is set:
> 
> ```typescript
> useEffect(() => {
>   if (!hasHydratedRuntimeState) return;
>   if (OPEN_HATCHERY_ON_LOAD) {
>     // Use the correct setter name found in Step B
>     setShowHatchery(true);
>     // Clean the URL param without a reload
>     const url = new URL(window.location.href);
>     url.searchParams.delete('openHatchery');
>     window.history.replaceState({}, '', url.toString());
>   }
> }, [hasHydratedRuntimeState]);
> ```
> 
> Replace `setShowHatchery` with the actual setter name found in Step B.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Constraints
> - Do **NOT** remove `CountdownCalendarModal` from `App.tsx` — just stop calling `setShowCalendarPlaceholder(true)` from `onDailyHatchClick`. Leave the modal and its state in place.
> - Do **NOT** modify any other handlers on `GameBoardOverlay` (Spin & Win, Hearts, Bank, Diamonds, Gold, Play).
> - The island scene image must not interfere with existing click handlers or z-index stacking.
> - Keep `opacity: 0.35` on the island scene image.
> - Do **NOT** introduce a new hatchery state variable — use the one that already exists in `IslandRunBoardPrototype.tsx`.
> 


</details>



