Adds a Stripe buy button to the navbar so it renders on every page, in both desktop and mobile views.

## Changes

- **`app/layout.tsx`**
  - Loads `https://js.stripe.com/v3/buy-button.js` via Next.js `<Script strategy="lazyOnload" />`
  - Extracts a `StripeBuyButton` component backed by module-level constants; falls back to hardcoded values if env vars are absent
  - Renders `<StripeBuyButton />` at the end of the desktop nav and inside the mobile dropdown

- **`types/stripe-buy-button.d.ts`** *(new)*
  - Augments `React.JSX.IntrinsicElements` so TypeScript accepts `<stripe-buy-button>` with its required attributes

```tsx
const STRIPE_BUY_BUTTON_ID =
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_BUY_BUTTON_ID ?? "buy_btn_1T6yYuDZfar9hiaNRjaBAsc1"
const STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY =
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY ?? "pk_live_..."

function StripeBuyButton() {
  return (
    <stripe-buy-button
      buy-button-id={STRIPE_BUY_BUTTON_ID}
      publishable-key={STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}
    ></stripe-buy-button>
  )
}
```

To override the defaults per environment, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_BUY_BUTTON_ID` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`.

